24. Practical applications

SFT can be instantiated as several operational modes.

Diagnostic mode maps local complaints, deltas, bottlenecks, attractors, and topology to locate the actual failure region.

Translation mode converts equivalent structures across personal dialects, professional domains, organizations, cultures, or machine representations.

Resource-routing mode maps needs, capabilities, resources, constraints, and pathways so resources become reachable by the entities that can use them.

Intervention mode finds the minimum sufficient change and the correct scale at which to apply it.

Simulation mode creates reversible branches before committing to costly changes.

Discovery mode searches unrelated domains for independently recurring operators.

Coordination mode selects when agents should lead, follow, support, synchronize, remain silent, or hand off control.

