26. Minimal computational prototype

A first implementation does not require continuous mathematics.

Use a dynamic attributed graph:

G_t=(V_t,E_t)

Each node stores:

(id,state,goals,constraints,resources,confidence,history)

Each edge stores:

(type,strength,direction,confidence,history)

Each observation produces:

Observation
\rightarrow
StateUpdate
\rightarrow
Delta
\rightarrow
PropagationEstimate

Each desired outcome invokes:

GoalSeek(target,G_t,constraints)

and returns candidate interventions ranked by:

cost,
reversibility,
reachability,
robustness,
uncertainty,
scale,
expected\ propagation

The first prototype should emphasize provenance and prediction logging over sophistication.

Every intervention records:

prediction_{before}

then:

observation_{after}

then:

delta

This prevents retrospective narrative from silently replacing prospective calibration.

